{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52056-cyberpunk-in-aeon","id":52056,"title":"Cyberpunk in Aeon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-17T18:53:11-08:00","id":52056,"title":"Cyberpunk in Aeon?","content":"In the previous version of Trinity, true cyberspace didn't exist. As the setting was designed, this made sense: After losing so much in the Optinet crash, why would mankind put all its eggs in one basket like that again?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, although sensible, this &quot;realistic&quot; option takes a FUN option off the table. And when those two collide, I go with &quot;fun&quot; every time! <br /> <br /> Is there a way to incorporate true Cyberspace play in Trinity? The easiest ways I can think of, setting-wise would be to say:<br /> <br /> 1) The Optinet survived the Aberrant War, and a more advanced version of it knits all the planets/space stations/etc man has spread to in Trinity. <br /> <br /> Or,<br /> <br /> 2) History did happen as before, but Trinity scientists, perhaps with help from their alien allies, came up with a new version of a &quot;spacenet&quot; that they're pretty sure is impervious to the previous disaster (although back up measures will still be taken, of course). <br /> <br /> I really don't care how it's done, I just want my Psion to be able to strap on a pair of googles, manifest her avatar in the digital world and hack my way from planetary node to planetary node! Is this feasible?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:06:34-08:00","id":52208,"title":"","content":"well, the opnet ran off eufiber, which was copied from, well, a very hairy nova who took his chest hair and became a fashion designer.<br /> <br /> Perhaps an Aeon scientist figures out a way to make biological computers that, in the same way the jumpships have the power to teleport, use artificial telepathy to transfer data. He reasons that since Novas can't manipulate psion particles, it's an unhackable system (at least by novas.) <br /> <br /> So you'd have big vat-grown cyborg brains in various places around the solar system 'talking' to each other. You could use the computer interface, but a psion could attune to one just like a bioapp to do a lot more.<br /> <br /> And since the books make allusions to big psion-crafted biomachines like the jumpships having a 'presence' almost like a living being, there's the potential for some wonky 'ghost in the machine' type antics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:43:21-08:00","id":52538,"title":"","content":"Looks like we will get a more flexible approach to tech in Aeon, especially connected tech such as minicomps, OpNet etc. John Snead (Aeon setting dude) recently suggested that there will be a different approach to how computer technology (including the OpNet) functions in the new Aeon game.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;I'm keeping this in mind for Aeon. Specifically, for hacking and electronics I want to go for options that increase both realism and fun. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">One example is that Aeon is a setting where people have been dealing with computer security for about as long as we've been using electric light - they know how to make it work. The best way to keep </span></span><b>really</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> secure is to keep it in a computer that's either entirely off-line or only connects to an isolated internal network. So, getting access to the super-secret plans or incriminating reports can't be done while hacking on your 22nd century smartphone/minicomp. Instead, you need to actually break into the high security installation and then either hack their internal network or gain physical access to the computer containing the data. That approach offers fun for the entire groups, while also making sense. Of course, there's also a bunch of less secure data that needs to be network accessible, and that can be hacked normally (although often not easily). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Also, wireless networks will be exactly as common you'd expect them - the limitations of wireless data do not exist in this version of Aeon (although there are other imposed limits on electronics), so PCs get to have their fancy smartphones.&quot;</span></span></i><br /> <br /> Swiped from the RPG.net thread here: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?713234-What-do-you-want-to-see-from-the-new-Trinity-Continuum&amp;p=17518606#post17518606\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...6#post17518606</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}